ot a safe tag, but it may have children (els or\n\n// text) that are, so recurse\n\nnumDiscarded\n++;\n\nnumDiscarded\n+= \ncopySafeNodes\n(\nsourceEl\n, \ndest\n);\n}\n} \nelse\n\nif\n(\nsourceChild\n\ninstanceof\n\nTextNode\n) {\n\nTextNode\n\nsourceText\n= (\nTextNode\n) \nsourceChild\n;\n\nTextNode\n\ndestText\n= \nnew\n\nTextNode\n(\nsourceText\n.\ngetWholeText\n(),\n\nsourceChild\n.\nbaseUri\n());\n\ndest\n.\nappendChild\n(\ndestText\n);\n} \n// else, we don't care about comments, xml proc instructions, etc\n\n}\n\nreturn\n\nnumDiscarded\n;\n}\n\nbut the clean result will be wrong and The layout will be chaos.\n\nHow can I solve this problem?"
